# Docs Shape

Every managed docs bucket follows this shape. Two profiles share most of
their structure; differences are flagged with **(service only)** or
**(library only)**.

## Profile detection

- `services/<svc>/docs/` → **service** profile.
- `docs/` at repo root, or `docs/` in a separate domain repo → **library**
  profile.

## PASSPORT.md is the anchor (service only)

In a service bucket, `PASSPORT.md` is the canonical service identity
record and the **first** file an agent should read when recalling
context for that service. Other docs in the bucket reference back to it.

PASSPORT.md is required (an audit error if missing). It carries:

- **YAML frontmatter at the top** — machine-readable identity:
  `service`, `domain`, `teams`, `network_dependencies`,
  `exposed_contracts`, plus deployment fields owned by the saas
  passport tooling.
- **Doc-meta header below the frontmatter** — same as every other
  managed doc.
- **Markdown body** — human-readable overview, deployment specs,
  environment variables, infrastructure dependencies, mermaid
  connection diagrams.

When the bucket lives in `services/<svc>/docs/`, an agent that needs to
understand or change the service should:

1. Read `services/<svc>/docs/PASSPORT.md` (identity, deps, contracts).
2. Read `services/<svc>/docs/README.md` (entry index).
3. Read `services/<svc>/docs/spec.md` and `backlog.md` (in-flight work).
4. Drill into `proposals/`, `adr/`, `guides/`, `reference/` as needed.

## Layout

```
<bucket>/
├── README.md           # overview + index, status: active                            (both)
├── PASSPORT.md         # service identity anchor — YAML frontmatter + body          (service only)
├── ROADMAP.md          # what's being built next (optional)                          (both)
├── spec.md             # testable acceptance criteria (⏳ → ✅)                       (service only)
├── backlog.md          # future work, ideas, deferred items                          (service only)
├── adr/                # immutable accepted decisions, NNN-slug.md                   (both)
├── proposals/          # designs, status: draft | decided                            (both)
├── guides/             # operational knowledge, how-tos, runbooks                    (both)
├── reference/          # contracts, schemas, env vars, API specs                     (both)
├── incidents/          # postmortems, YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md (optional)                  (both)
└── archive/            # superseded proposals, guides, reference (read-only)        (both)
    ├── proposals/
    ├── guides/
    └── reference/
```

Do not create new top-level folders or files here. If a real need
appears, write a proposal first. **Library buckets must not contain
PASSPORT.md, spec.md, or backlog.md** — those are service-only artifacts.

## Mandatory header on every managed doc

```markdown
<!-- doc-meta -->
> **Status:** draft | active | accepted | superseded | archived
> **Type:** overview | passport | roadmap | spec | backlog | proposal | adr | guide | reference | incident
> **Owner:** <gitlab handle or team>
> **Updated:** YYYY-MM-DD
```

For PASSPORT.md, the doc-meta header sits **after** the YAML frontmatter:

```markdown
---
service: <name>
domain: <domain>
teams: [<team>]
network_dependencies:
  outbound: { ... }
  inbound: [ ... ]
exposed_contracts:
  grpc: [ ... ]
  nats: { publishes: [...], subscribes: [...] }
  rest: { base: "", endpoints: [] }
---
<!-- doc-meta -->
> **Status:** active
> **Type:** passport
> **Owner:** <team>
> **Updated:** YYYY-MM-DD

# <Service Name> Service Passport
...
```

The plugin only checks YAML *parses* and the four doc-meta fields are
present. Schema details for the passport YAML are owned by the saas
passport tooling (`service-passport-agent-context` skill).

Without the doc-meta header, a file in any bucket is not a managed doc.
When creating or moving a doc, write the header. When updating one, bump
`Updated`.

## Naming

| Folder / file | Pattern |
|---------------|---------|
| `adr/` | `NNN-slug.md` (zero-padded, e.g. `001-grpc-migration.md`) |
| `incidents/` | `YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md` |
| `proposals/`, `guides/`, `reference/`, `archive/**` | `kebab-case.md` |
| Top-level | `README.md`, `PASSPORT.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `spec.md`, `backlog.md` (fixed names) |

## Lifecycle transitions

| Type | Transitions | Notes |
|------|-------------|-------|
| **PASSPORT** *(service only)* | always `active`; rewritten on identity / deps / contracts change | bump `Updated`; never archived (a service either has one or doesn't exist) |
| Spec items *(service only)* | `⏳` → `✅` | Each AC is a checkbox. Flip when done. Never delete completed items. |
| Backlog items *(service only)* | bullet → `spec.md` | When work begins, move into `spec.md` with `⏳` markers. |
| Proposal | `draft` → `decided` (paired ADR) | Once decided, link the ADR; stop editing the body. |
| Proposal | `draft` → `archived` (move to `archive/proposals/`) | Leave a tombstone. |
| ADR | `accepted` → `superseded by ADR-NNN` | Old ADR's body is immutable; only the status line is edited. |
| Guide | `active` → `archived` (move to `archive/guides/`) | Retired guides keep their history accessible. |
| Reference | drift → fix same day | Reference docs name their source file in code. |
| Incident | append-only after creation | New findings appended with a timestamped section; existing sections never rewritten. |

## Spec-driven workflow (service only)

`spec.md` is the testable contract for what the service is delivering
right now. Each AC is a checkbox with `⏳` (pending) or `✅` (done):

```markdown
- [ ] ⏳ POST /transactions returns 201 on valid payload
- [x] ✅ POST /transactions returns 400 on missing currency
```

Workflow: pick from `backlog.md` → translate to checkbox AC in `spec.md`
with `⏳` → implement → flip to `✅` → bump `Updated`. Non-trivial
design choices become a proposal under `proposals/`, paired with an ADR
when decided.

## Forbidden

- Creating a doc in any bucket without the doc-meta header.
- Editing the body of an `accepted` ADR.
- Editing files under `archive/` except to add a redirect.
- Mixing types in a folder (e.g. ADRs in `proposals/`).
- Cross-service docs in a single service's bucket.
- Library-bucket-specific artifacts (`PASSPORT.md`, `spec.md`,
  `backlog.md`) appearing in a library bucket.
- Service-specific content in a library bucket. If the doc describes a
  single service, it belongs in `services/<svc>/docs/`.
- Deleting completed (`✅`) AC from `spec.md` to "clean up".
- Rewriting an `accepted` PASSPORT yaml frontmatter without bumping
  `Updated` and reflecting the change in the markdown body.

## Skills

- `docs-setup` — bootstrap any bucket (asks profile, creates PASSPORT
  for service buckets).
- `docs-lifecycle` — every create / promote / supersede / archive
  action, including PASSPORT updates.
- `docs-audit` — validate an existing bucket and autofix safe issues;
  flags missing PASSPORT for service buckets as an error.
